==============================================================================
S2-1b  competing locality criteria on the same abstract dynamics
==============================================================================

--- 0. Minimal k without a supplied number of factors (N = 16) ---
  random H, 1 factor (16)   : k = 1  (#factors 1)
  random H, 4 (x) 4         : k = 2  (#factors 2)
  random H, 2 (x) 8         : k = 2  (#factors 2)
  random H, 2 (x) 2 (x) 4   : k = 3  (#factors 3)
  random H, 2^4 qubits      : k = 4  (#factors 4)
  => over all factorizations minimal k is won by the TRIVIAL factorization (k = 1). The criterion is
     ill-posed unless the number of factors or the local dimension is supplied (finest = prime: 2^4).

--- Case A. N = 16: strong generic pair terms + weak bridge.  H = h12 + h34 + g X2 X3 ---
  TPS                                k     edges       mdl        lr      loc2      auto
  qubits 2(x)2(x)2(x)2               2         3        39    0.0815       1.0    0.5059
  ququarts 4(x)4                     2         1       255    0.0002       1.0    0.9997
  2 (x) 8                            2         1       255    0.1579       1.0    0.8087
    minimal k                      -> qubits 2(x)2(x)2(x)2   (TIE with ququarts 4(x)4, 2 (x) 8)
    sparse graph (edge fraction)   -> qubits 2(x)2(x)2(x)2
    Lieb-Robinson                  -> ququarts 4(x)4
    MDL                            -> qubits 2(x)2(x)2(x)2
    locality-max                   -> qubits 2(x)2(x)2(x)2   (TIE with ququarts 4(x)4, 2 (x) 8)
    autonomy                       -> ququarts 4(x)4

--- Case B. n = 5 qubits, same local dimension, same #factors; TPS2 = Clifford-rotated frame ---

  H = transverse-field Ising chain (2-local NN): 1500 random Clifford frames; strict exact-criterion disagreement patterns: 0

  H = 3-body ZZZ chain + X fields: 1500 random Clifford frames; strict exact-criterion disagreement patterns: 1

  pattern: rotated frame BETTER on ('mdl',), WORSE on ('edges',)
  TPS                                k     edges       mdl        lr      loc2      auto
  computational                      3         7       159     0.074    0.6999    0.6999
  Clifford-rotated                   3         8       141    0.1038    0.8518    0.2267
    minimal k                      -> computational   (TIE with Clifford-rotated)
    sparse graph (edge fraction)   -> computational
    Lieb-Robinson                  -> computational
    MDL                            -> Clifford-rotated
    locality-max                   -> Clifford-rotated
    autonomy                       -> computational

--- Stability (Case A). Perturb H -> H + eps V. Which measure for V? ---
  V ~ GUE (TPS-neutral)      eps=0.001 : k q/Q = 4/2, MDL q/Q = 255/255, loc2 q/Q = 1.000/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.506/1.000
  V ~ GUE (TPS-neutral)      eps=0.1   : k q/Q = 4/2, MDL q/Q = 255/255, loc2 q/Q = 0.993/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.510/0.991
  V ~ 2-local in QUBIT TPS   eps=0.001 : k q/Q = 2/2, MDL q/Q = 66/255, loc2 q/Q = 1.000/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.506/1.000
  V ~ 2-local in QUBIT TPS   eps=0.1   : k q/Q = 2/2, MDL q/Q = 66/255, loc2 q/Q = 1.000/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.501/0.992
  V ~ local in QUQUART TPS   eps=0.001 : k q/Q = 2/2, MDL q/Q = 39/255, loc2 q/Q = 1.000/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.506/1.000
  V ~ local in QUQUART TPS   eps=0.1   : k q/Q = 2/2, MDL q/Q = 39/255, loc2 q/Q = 1.000/1.000, auto q/Q = 0.494/1.000
  => exact criteria (k, edges, MDL) are destroyed by any TPS-neutral perturbation; they 'survive' only under a
     perturbation measure that is itself local in a chosen TPS (circular). Weighted criteria survive but still
     disagree (loc2 vs autonomy). STABILITY IS MEASURE-PRICED.
